From: fcfb project
Subject: [PATCH] net: macb: enable jumbo frames on Zynq-7000 (GEM)

The Cadence GEM on the Zynq-7000 supports jumbo frames but the mainline
zynq_config leaves them disabled, capping MTU at 1500. fcfb streams selected
FFT bins as datagram-atomic UDP records at 40k blocks/s; at MTU 1500 a record
over ~1460 B fragments and the doubled packet rate collapses throughput. Enable
MACB_CAPS_JUMBO with jumbo_max_len=10240 (max_mtu becomes min(10240,16320)-18 =
10222) so the board can egress larger unfragmented datagrams. Per Pavel Demin
(RedPitaya forum t=25577) the board->host (TX-from-GEM) direction sustains
~960 Mbit/s at raised MTU; host->board (RX) may misbehave above ~2340, but for
fcfb that direction carries only tiny TCP control requests.

Signed-off-by: fcfb project <fcfb@localhost>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/cadence/macb_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/cadence/macb_main.c
@@ -5637,8 +5637,10 @@
 static const struct macb_config zynq_config = {
 	.caps = MACB_CAPS_GIGABIT_MODE_AVAILABLE | MACB_CAPS_NO_GIGABIT_HALF |
 		MACB_CAPS_NEEDS_RSTONUBR |
+		MACB_CAPS_JUMBO |
 		MACB_CAPS_USRIO_HAS_MII,
 	.dma_burst_length = 16,
+	.jumbo_max_len = 10240,
 	.usrio = &at91_default_usrio,
 };
 
